Embedded React: a per-font coverage gamma for baked fonts.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: bridges/quickjs/js/assets/bake-font.mjs,
bridges/quickjs/js/assets/font-config.mjs and
bridges/quickjs/js/assets/__tests__/assets.unit.test.js. Not yet proposed
upstream.

The engine blends glyph coverage in sRGB, so antialiased stems read lighter
than on a renderer that blends in linear light: SST titles measured about half
a weight under the PS5's own UI at the same font, weight and size. A font's
`gamma` in assets.config.js (default 1, unchanged) lifts each baked pixel's
coverage to 255 * (cov / 255)^(1 / gamma) before packing, at no runtime cost.
Empty and full pixels keep their values; gamma must be 0.5 to 4.

